# EXCLUDED FROM THE BUILD 2026-08-20 (Ray's call, on GitNexus's precedent).
# Not a de-registration: the pin above stays committed and fingerprinted, so
# provenance is intact and this stays on the record as what it was FOR.
# `kb-build` fails closed here on 233 partially-extracted files. The reviewed
# inventory is per-file and content-hash-pinned by design, so clearing it by
# hand means 233 measured entries — at the ~10-15 min per entry this round
# measured, tens of hours. That is #409 ("the reviewed-warning inventories do
# not scale"), the same wall GitNexus hit at 94.
#
# It also buys nothing: 877 of the 1,496 `.c`/`.h` files sit under
# `internal/cbm/vendored/` and are vendored tree-sitter grammar headers —
# third-party C inside a third-party clone, not the study subject's own code —
# and `scope = study` already keeps this source out of the aggregate.
# Restore by deleting these two lines once #409 lands.
